        "stem": "Which option best combines these sentences into one correct sentence? “The museum closed early. The staff needed to repair a broken window.”",
        "options": [
          {
            "text": "The museum closed early because the staff needed to repair a broken window.",
            "isKey": true,
            "misconception": null,
            "rationale": "This sentence clearly shows that the repair work was the reason for the early closure."
          },
          {
            "text": "The museum closed early, but the staff needed to repair a broken window.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "MISUSES_CONTRAST_CONNECTOR",
            "rationale": "“But” suggests a contrast, but repairing the window explains the closure rather than contrasting with it."
          },
          {
            "text": "The museum closed early, the staff needing to repair a broken window.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "COMMA_SPLICE",
            "rationale": "This joins two complete ideas with a comma in an unclear way instead of showing the cause clearly."
          },
          {
            "text": "The museum closed early although the staff needed to repair a broken window.",
            "isKey": false,
            "misconception": "MISUSES_CONCESSION_CONNECTOR",
            "rationale": "“Although” suggests that the repair need should not have caused the closure, which does not match the meaning."
          }
        ],
        "evidenceQuote": null
